# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/night_market.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event nm_rumour
# en: A Field That Isn't Empty
title [8c6301] = 不空的田野
# en: {~At the well, two old women are arguing about the far field past the last stile. "No moon tonight," says one. "They'll be out after twelve." "There's nothing out there," says the other, "and don't you go buying from it."|The baker's girl, wrapping your bun, asks if you're going "out to the far field" after midnight, "with it being no moon". Seeing your face, she goes red and says she meant nothing.|A pedlar's cart rattles out of the square towards the far field, hung with unlit lanterns. A boy on the wall says it's the market, the one that comes after midnight on moonless nights.}
text [ee3a8d] = {~井边，两个老太太正为最后一道篱阶外的那片远田争个不停。“今晚没月亮，”一个说，“过了十二点他们就会出来。”“那儿什么也没有，”另一个说，“你可别去那儿买东西。”|面包房的姑娘一边给你包小面包，一边问你午夜后是不是要“去远田”，“反正今晚没月亮”。看到你的表情，她脸一红，说自己什么也没说。|一辆小贩的车子挂着没点的灯笼，咣当咣当地出了广场，往远田去了。墙头上一个男孩说，那是集市，没月亮的夜里过了午夜才来的那个。}
# en: A village square, two old women at a well, one pointing past the rooftops towards a dark field.
scene [97cbb2] = 村庄广场，两个老太太站在井边，其中一个指着屋顶那头一片黑黢黢的田野。
# en: Ask what they sell out there
opt.left.label [b82f64] = 问问那儿卖什么
# en: {~"Anything," says the first old woman. "Lanterns. Dreams. Bad bargains." The second one tells you about her nephew, who sold his singing voice there, at length, until you have to run for the barge.|"Candles that burn the wrong way," the baker's girl whispers, "and worse. My gran bought back a year once." She won't say any more, and you've missed the barge.|"Everything they shouldn't," says the boy. He tells you about a man who bought a door, asks you for a coin, and runs off before you can say no.}
opt.left.say.1 [b95337] = {~“什么都卖，”第一个老太太说，“灯笼、梦、亏本的买卖。”第二个则讲起她的外甥，说他在那儿把自己的歌喉卖了，讲了好久，直到你不得不跑去赶驳船。|“倒着烧的蜡烛，”面包房的姑娘小声说，“还有更糟的。我奶奶有一回在那儿买回了一年。”她不肯再说，你也误了驳船。|“什么不该卖的都卖，”男孩说。他给你讲了个买了一扇门的人，然后问你要一枚硬币，没等你说不就跑了。}
# en: Keep walking
opt.right.label [6ca967] = 接着走
# en: {~You fill your water and go. The far field, past the stile, after twelve: you put it away somewhere, in case.|You take your bun and don't ask. It stays with you anyway, all the way back across the lake.|You watch the cart go and turn back to the square. You'll remember the field, whether you mean to or not.}
opt.right.say.1 [24d787] = {~你打满了水就走。远田，篱阶外，十二点以后：你把它收在心里某个角落，以防万一。|你拿了小面包，什么也没问。可这事一路跟着你，跟着你过了湖。|你看着车子远去，转身回到广场。那片田，你想不记得也得记得。}

@event nm_rumour_newt
# en: Coin That Isn't From Here
title [8b8cba] = 不是这儿的硬币
# en: {~The landlady holds a coin up to the lamp: square, with a hole in it and a moon on one side. "Third one this month," she says. "Every moonless night somebody goes out to the far field after twelve, and comes back paying me in these."|A regular slaps a square coin with a hole in it on the bar and asks if it's good for a cider. The landlady sighs. "Been out past the stile again, have you. Moonless nights, midnight, every month the school's in."|An old bargeman is telling the bar about the market in the far field, past the last stile, after midnight on a moonless night, and a woman there who sold him back a song he'd forgotten. Nobody laughs.}
text [9f536c] = {~老板娘把一枚硬币举到灯下：方的，中间有个孔，一面刻着月亮。“这个月第三枚了，”她说，“每个没月亮的夜里，总有人十二点后去远田，回来就拿这个付我账。”|一位常客把一枚带孔的方硬币拍在吧台上，问能不能换一杯苹果酒。老板娘叹了口气：“又去篱阶外头了吧。没月亮的夜，半夜，学校开学的每个月都有。”|一个老驳船夫正跟满吧台的人讲远田里的集市：最后一道篱阶外，没月亮的夜里过了午夜才有；那儿有个女人把他早忘了的一首歌又卖还给了他。没人笑。}
# en: A tavern bar at night, a landlady holding a strange coin up to the lamp, a regular grinning over his cider.
scene [f8711c] = 夜里的酒馆吧台，老板娘把一枚奇怪的硬币举到灯下，一位常客对着苹果酒咧嘴笑。
# en: Buy a round for the rest of it
opt.left.label [e89eb0] = 请大家喝一轮，听完整个故事
# en: {~The regulars drink to you and tell you the rest: hooded sellers, no prices until you ask, a stall nobody minds. "Take coin," one of them says, "and don't take anything else they offer you. Or do. I did."|For a cider you get the whole of it, down to the stall that sells lanterns lit from the seller's thumb. He won't say what he bought.|The landlady tells you the rest herself, to stop him telling it worse. "Mind your purse," she says, "and mind your name."}
opt.left.say.1 [9f5c73] = {~常客们举杯敬你，把剩下的都讲给你听：戴兜帽的卖家，不问就不报价，还有一个没人看管的摊子。“收硬币，”其中一个说，“别的什么都别收。要不就收，我收过。”|一杯苹果酒换来了全部，连那个用拇指点灯笼的摊子都讲到了。他就是不肯说自己买了什么。|老板娘干脆自己讲完，免得他越讲越离谱。“看好你的钱袋，”她说，“也看好你的名字。”}
# en: Leave them to their stories
opt.right.label [623a8e] = 让他们自己讲去
# en: {~You finish your drink. Every tavern has a field something happens in, but you remember where this one is.|The story gets taller as you leave. By the door it has a dragon in it. The stile and the midnight stay with you, though.|You let it go, and the square coin goes back in the till. You think about it on the barge.}
opt.right.say.1 [ff84f6] = {~你喝完了酒。每家酒馆都有一片出过怪事的田，可这一片在哪儿，你记住了。|你往外走时，故事越讲越高。到门口时里面已经有了一条龙。可篱阶和午夜，你都记下了。|你没再理会，那枚方硬币也回到了钱柜里。坐驳船回去时，你一直在想它。}

@event night_market_stalls
# en: The Night Market
title [8fbd8e] = 夜市
# en: {~Past the last stile, the far field is full of stalls, lit green and violet and a blue that has no business being a flame. Nobody calls out prices. You have to ask.|The far field is all stalls and smoke and the smell of cloves, hooded sellers behind every one, and not a price written anywhere.|No moon, and the far field is lit from end to end. A hooded seller lifts a hand to you as if you were expected.} {~On one cloth, a candle is burning upwards into itself.|A woman with no lantern at all sells lanterns.|Somebody is weighing a bag of moonlight on brass scales and arguing about the result.}
text [78cf75] = {~过了最后一道篱阶，远田里满是摊位，亮着绿的、紫的，还有一种根本不该是火焰的蓝。没人吆喝价钱。你得自己问。|远田里全是摊位、烟和丁香味，每个摊后都站着戴兜帽的卖家，哪儿也没写价钱。|没有月亮，远田从这头亮到那头。一个戴兜帽的卖家朝你抬了抬手，好像早在等你。} {~一块布上，一支蜡烛正往上烧回它自己。|一个手里没提灯的女人在卖灯笼。|有人在用黄铜秤称一袋月光，正为结果争吵。}
# en: A field at midnight full of stalls lit by coloured flames, hooded sellers, and a candle on a cloth burning the wrong way up.
scene [a796a2] = 午夜的田野里满是亮着彩色火焰的摊位，戴兜帽的卖家，一块布上一支蜡烛倒着燃烧。
# en: A lantern of blue flame
opt.lantern.label [fa2d14] = 一盏蓝火灯笼
# en: It lights a way home nobody else can see: whoever noticed you slip out tonight forgets it.
opt.lantern.hint [dda86e] = 它照出一条别人看不见的回家路：今晚谁看见你溜出去，都会忘掉。
# en: {~The lantern-woman lights it from her thumb. All the way back, the flame shows you doors that are open and stairs that are empty, and nothing else.|It burns blue and makes no shadow. You come in by a door you didn't know about and are in bed before the bell.|"Home," she tells the flame, and it goes, and you follow it. In the morning the lantern is a cold glass ball.}
opt.lantern.say.1 [ab39b0] = {~卖灯的女人用拇指点着了它。一路回去，那团火只照出开着的门和空着的楼梯，别的什么也不照。|它烧着蓝光，不投影子。你从一扇从不知道的门进去，钟还没响就已躺在床上。|“回家，”她对火说。火便走，你便跟着。第二天早上，灯笼成了一只冰冷的玻璃球。}
# en: A candle that burns backwards
opt.candle.label [85c562] = 一支倒着烧的蜡烛
# en: It gives back the night it burns: you'll sleep as if you'd never gone out.
opt.candle.hint [c75240] = 它燃尽的那一夜会还给你：你会睡得像从没出过门。
# en: {~You light it by your bed. It grows taller as it burns, and in the morning you've slept the whole night you spent in a field.|The flame burns down into the wick and the wax climbs back up. You wake rested and slightly unnerved.|It burns backwards for an hour, and your tiredness goes with it. The candle is new again by morning, and you can't bring yourself to light it twice.}
opt.candle.say.1 [c7d0ce] = {~你在床边点着它。它越烧越高，到早上，你在田野里度过的那一整夜都睡回来了。|火焰往灯芯里烧下去，蜡却往上长回来。你醒来时神清气爽，又有点发毛。|它倒着烧了一个钟头，你的疲倦也跟着去了。到早上蜡烛又是新的，你却怎么也下不了手再点一次。}
# en: A bottled dream (someone else's)
opt.dream.label [eaef2b] = 一瓶装着的梦（别人的）
# en: A night in a stranger's dream: you'll know a little more, and sleep a little worse.
opt.dream.hint [3f18fb] = 在陌生人的梦里过一夜：你会多知道一点，也会睡得差一点。
# en: {~You dream of a harbour you've never seen and a language you nearly understand. You wake low and far from home, with three words of it still on your tongue.|You dream an old man's dream of a library with no doors, and wake strangely sad. But you know where a book is kept that you've never read.|Someone else's dream, worn soft at the edges: a kitchen, a voice, a recipe. You wake homesick for a home that isn't yours.}
opt.dream.say.1 [36e269] = {~你梦见一个从没见过的港口，和一种差一点就能听懂的语言。醒来时你心情低落，远离家乡，舌尖上还留着其中三个词。|你做了一个老人的梦，梦里是一座没有门的图书馆，醒来时莫名地难过。可你知道了一本从没读过的书放在哪儿。|别人的梦，边角都磨软了：一间厨房，一个声音，一份食谱。你醒来时想家，想的却是一个不属于你的家。}
# en: The pedlar's black bottle
opt.ink.label [8e2c3b] = 小贩的黑瓶子
# en: Owl's Ink, the banned exam elixir: a sharp head for a while, and a habit if you let it.
opt.ink.hint [fafac4] = 枭墨，禁用的考试药剂：头脑能清醒一阵子，你若放任，也会成瘾。
# en: {~The pedlar doesn't take it out from under his coat until your coin is in his hand. Black and bitter, and dearer than it should be.|"Exams coming?" says the pedlar, who can't possibly know. He wraps the black bottle in a page of an old almanac.|He sells it to you without a word, and you wrap it in your scarf and walk home faster than you came.}
opt.ink.say.1 [9d614a] = {~硬币进了小贩的手，他才把它从大衣底下拿出来。又黑又苦，贵得不该这么贵。|“快考试了？”小贩说，他不可能知道。他用一页旧年历把黑瓶子包了起来。|他一言不发地卖给你。你用围巾把它裹好，回去的路走得比来时快。}
# en: Walk the stalls and buy nothing
opt.walk.label [c5705e] = 逛遍摊位，什么也不买
# en: {~You walk the rows twice, slowly. Nobody minds. The smell of cloves stays in your robes for days.|You watch a woman buy a song and carry it away in her cupped hands. You don't buy anything. You'll think about it for a week.|You warm your hands at a green fire and walk home under no moon at all.}
opt.walk.say.1 [06d454] = {~你慢慢地把每一排走了两遍。没人在意。丁香味在你的长袍上留了好几天。|你看着一个女人买下一首歌，用捧着的双手把它带走。你什么也没买。这事你会想上一个星期。|你在一堆绿火边暖了暖手，在全然无月的夜里走回去。}

@event nm_memory_tuner
# en: Payment in Kind
title [706112] = 以物抵价
# en: {~A wand-tuner holds out a hand for your wand, listens to it like a doctor listening to a chest, and hands it back. "Flat," she says. "I'll tune it. I don't take coin. I take one memory: a small one, your choice. The jar's for that."|A tuner's stall of forks and wands, and an empty jar. The woman behind it takes your wand without asking and holds it to her ear. "Flat," she says. "One memory, and it sings."|"Your wand's singing a quarter-note low," says the tuner. She taps the empty jar. "One small memory and it sings true. You'll never miss it. Mostly."}
text [c8f9a5] = {~一位调杖师伸手要你的魔杖，像医生听胸口那样听了听，又还给你。“走音了，”她说，“我来调。我不收钱。我收一段记忆：小小的一段，你自己挑。那个罐子就是装它的。”|一个摆满音叉和魔杖的调杖摊，还有一只空罐子。摊后的女人不问一声就拿过你的魔杖，凑到耳边。“走音了，”她说，“一段记忆，它就能唱准。”|“你的魔杖低了四分之一个音，”调杖师说。她敲了敲那只空罐子。“一小段记忆，它就唱得准了。你不会想念它的。大概吧。”}
# en: A hooded wand-tuner at a stall of tuning forks and wands, a small glass jar on the counter, empty and waiting.
scene [bbd351] = 一个戴兜帽的调杖师守着摆满音叉和魔杖的摊子，柜台上一只小玻璃罐，空着，等着。
# en: Give her a small memory
opt.left.label [c36206] = 给她一小段记忆
# en: {~You think of a summer afternoon, and it goes into the jar like smoke. Your wand rings true. You can't now remember what the afternoon was, only that it was nice.|You give her the taste of a pie your grandmother used to make. The wand sings like a bell. Later you sit in the refectory trying to remember why you're sad.|She takes the first time you rode a barge. The wand is wonderful. You feel, for a day or two, a little less like someone who has been somewhere.}
opt.left.say.1 [863dff] = {~你想起一个夏日午后，它像烟一样飘进罐子。你的魔杖响得准了。你如今记不起那个午后是什么样了，只记得很好。|你把奶奶做的那种馅饼的味道给了她。魔杖唱得像钟一样。后来你坐在膳堂里，想不起自己为什么难过。|她拿走了你第一次坐驳船的记忆。魔杖棒极了。可有那么一两天，你觉得自己不太像一个去过什么地方的人了。}
# en: Keep your memories
opt.right.label [d32952] = 留着你的记忆
# en: {~You take your flat wand home and your memories with you. On the way you go through them, one by one, to be sure they're all there.|"Suit yourself," says the tuner. "Flat's a kind of honest." You find yourself agreeing.|You walk away holding on to something, though you couldn't say what. It feels worth it.}
opt.right.say.1 [3f6f9d] = {~你把走音的魔杖和你的记忆一起带回去。路上你一段一段地翻检，确认它们都还在。|“随你，”调杖师说，“走音也算一种诚实。”你发觉自己同意她。|你走开时紧紧攥着什么，却说不出是什么。觉得值得。}

@event nm_stolen_compass
# en: A Name You Know
title [72b8c7] = 一个你认识的名字
# en: {~On a cloth of oddments lies a little silver compass. The name engraved on the lid is a first-year's; you heard her crying about it in the refectory a week ago.|On a cloth of oddments lies a music box with a second-year's name scratched inside the lid. He's been asking the whole castle about it for a month.|Among the spoons and buckles on one cloth is a signet ring you've seen on a classmate's hand since your first week. She's been in tears about it since Tuesday.}
text [47ad00] = {~一块摆着杂物的布上躺着一只小银罗盘。盖子上刻的名字是一个一年级生的；一个星期前你还听见她在膳堂里为它哭。|一块摆着杂物的布上放着一只八音盒，盒盖内侧刻着一个二年级生的名字。他已经满城堡打听了它一个月。|一块布上的勺子和扣子中间，有一枚图章戒指，你从入学第一周起就天天在一个同学手上看见它。她从星期二起就一直在哭。}
# en: A cloth spread with oddments at a night stall, one of them engraved with a name, beside a seller who won't meet your eye.
scene [47185a] = 夜市摊上铺着一块杂物布，其中一件刻着名字，摊主不肯看你的眼睛。
# en: Buy it back for its owner
opt.left.label [fc2291] = 替失主买回来
# en: {~The seller wants more than it's worth and gets it. In the morning you hand it back at breakfast and say where you found it. Its owner tells the whole table.|You pay. The seller looks almost sorry. At breakfast its owner holds it as if it might vanish again, and by lunch half the castle knows who brought it back.|You buy it and give it back at breakfast. You get a hug you weren't ready for, and the story is round the refectory before the porridge is cold.}
opt.left.say.1 [9ac021] = {~摊主要价比它值的多，也真要到了。第二天早饭时你把它还了回去，说了是在哪儿找到的。失主讲给了整桌人听。|你付了钱。摊主看上去几乎有点过意不去。早饭时失主捧着它，好像它还会再消失似的；到午饭时，半个城堡都知道是谁把它带回来的了。|你买下它，早饭时还了回去。你挨了一个没准备好的拥抱，粥还没凉，这事已经传遍了膳堂。}
# en: Bluff him out of it
opt.right.label [b41362] = 诈他交出来
# en: {~You tell him the castle porter keeps a list of everything stolen from the school, and you've seen this on it. He gives it to you for nothing and is gone before you look up.|You say, loudly, that its owner is a prefect's sibling. He pushes it into your hand and takes his cloth away.|You lie beautifully about a curse on stolen keepsakes. The seller can't get rid of it fast enough. Its owner never asks how you got it back.}
opt.right.say.1 [5b5aa5] = {~你告诉他，城堡的门房有一张学校所有失窃物品的清单，你在上面见过这件。他一分钱没要就给了你，你一抬头他已经不见了。|你大声说它的主人是一位级长的兄弟姐妹。他把它塞进你手里，卷起布就走。|你绘声绘色地编了个关于偷来的信物会招诅咒的故事。摊主恨不得马上脱手。失主从没问过你是怎么拿回来的。}
# en: {~He doesn't believe a word and says so, loudly, and heads turn all down the row. You leave empty-handed and with your face burning.|The seller laughs, folds his cloth and moves three stalls down. You saw where, but it doesn't help.|"Prove it," he says. You can't, at midnight, in a field. He puts it in his pocket.}
opt.right.say.2 [cefd22] = {~他一个字也不信，还大声说出来，整排摊子的人都转过头来。你空着手走开，脸上火辣辣的。|摊主笑了，卷起布挪到了三个摊位外。你看见了在哪儿，可那也没用。|“证明给我看，”他说。半夜里，在田野中，你证明不了。他把它揣进了口袋。}

@event nm_thornwick_shopper
# en: Green Robes in the Dark
title [f08b4b] = 黑暗里的绿袍
# en: {~Across the lanterns, a student in Thornwick green is haggling for a bag of something that glitters. She sees your robes. You see hers. You're both a very long way past curfew.|A Thornwick boy in a borrowed hood is buying the same blue lantern you were looking at. He freezes when he sees your Lumenhold cuffs.|Thornwick green, under a hood, at the sweet stall. She raises a toffee apple to you like a toast, and waits to see what you'll do.}
text [0af692] = {~隔着灯笼，一个穿荆木绿袍的学生正为一袋闪闪发光的东西讨价还价。她看见了你的长袍，你也看见了她的。你们俩都早已远远过了宵禁。|一个戴着借来兜帽的荆木男生正在买你刚才看中的那盏蓝灯笼。看到你的流明堡袖口，他僵住了。|兜帽下一抹荆木绿，在糖果摊前。她朝你举起一只太妃糖苹果，像是在敬酒，等着看你怎么做。}
# en: A student in Thornwick green under a hood at a night-market stall, caught mid-bargain, staring at a Lumenhold student across the lanterns.
scene [07b5a9] = 夜市摊前，一个穿荆木绿袍、戴着兜帽的学生正讨价还价到一半，隔着灯笼盯着一个流明堡学生。
# en: Swap a secret for a secret
opt.left.label [92fc49] = 拿一个秘密换一个秘密
# en: {~You tell her where the Lumenhold kitchens leave the door unlatched. She tells you which Thornwick tutor sets the exchange examinations, and what he always asks.|A trade, over toffee: your school's night porter's habits for the name of their best duellist's bad knee. Neither of you feels very good about it.|He tells you something useful about Thornwick's spring exams. You tell him which Lumenhold porter sleeps through the ten o'clock bell, and regret it on the walk home.}
opt.left.say.1 [d03d42] = {~你告诉她流明堡的厨房哪扇门不上门闩。她告诉你哪位荆木导师出交换生考试，他总爱问什么。|就着太妃糖做了笔交易：你们学校夜班门房的习惯，换他们最好的决斗手那只伤膝盖的名字。你们俩谁心里都不太舒坦。|他告诉你一些荆木春季考试的有用消息。你告诉他流明堡哪个门房总睡过十点的钟声，回去的路上就后悔了。}
# en: Pretend you never saw each other
opt.right.label [ddeb3a] = 假装谁也没看见谁
# en: {~You both look at the sky until the moment passes. When you look back she's gone, and the stallholder is laughing.|You nod. He nods. You walk off in opposite directions, both much more careful than you were a minute ago.|You raise a toffee apple back. Nobody says a word, and it's the friendliest thing that's happened between the two schools all year.}
opt.right.say.1 [276cba] = {~你们俩都抬头看天，直到那一刻过去。再低头时她已经走了，摊主在笑。|你点点头，他也点点头。你们朝相反的方向走开，都比一分钟前小心多了。|你也举起一只太妃糖苹果回敬。谁也没说话，这是两校今年发生过的最友好的事。}

@event nm_honesty_stall
# en: Nobody Minding the Stall
title [a2a4fb] = 没人看管的摊子
# en: {~One stall has no seller at all: apples, loaves, a candle and a wooden bowl for coins. Every time you look away, the candle seems to have moved.|At the end of a row, a stall with apples, loaves, a candle and a bowl, and nobody behind it. You look away and back, and the bowl is on the other side.|A stall with nobody minding it: bread, apples, a bowl for coins. People walk past it without looking, the way you'd walk past a dog that bites.}
text [c85b57] = {~有一个摊子根本没有摊主：苹果、面包、一支蜡烛，和一只放硬币的木碗。你每次移开视线，蜡烛好像都挪了位置。|一排摊子的尽头，有个摆着苹果、面包、一支蜡烛和一只碗的摊子，后面没人。你移开视线再看回来，碗已经到了另一边。|一个没人看管的摊子：面包、苹果、一只收钱的碗。人们从它旁边走过，看都不看，就像走过一条会咬人的狗。}
# en: An unattended night stall of apples and loaves by a single candle, with a wooden bowl for coins and no seller anywhere.
scene [eadb54] = 一个无人看管的夜间摊位，一支蜡烛照着苹果和面包，一只收钱的木碗，四下不见摊主。
# en: Pay for an apple, honestly
opt.left.label [012dd5] = 老老实实付钱买个苹果
# en: {~You drop a coin in the bowl. The apple is the best you've ever eaten, and somewhere behind you someone says "thank you" who isn't there.|Your coin rings in the empty bowl. The candle flickers in a way that looks very much like a nod.|You pay, and take an apple. It's warm, as if it had been in the sun, at midnight.}
opt.left.say.1 [74fc23] = {~你往碗里放了一枚硬币。那是你吃过最好的苹果，身后某处有个不在场的人说了声“谢谢”。|你的硬币在空碗里叮当一响。烛火晃了晃，看上去很像点了点头。|你付了钱，拿了一个苹果。它是温的，像是晒过太阳，可这是半夜。}
# en: Take an apple and go
opt.right.label [c56046] = 拿个苹果就走
# en: {~You take one. Nothing happens. All the way home you keep turning round, and nothing keeps happening.|You take an apple. It's sour, very sour, and you finish it out of stubbornness.|You take one and walk off quickly. When you look back the stall's gone, bowl and candle and all.}
opt.right.say.1 [ab923f] = {~你拿了一个。什么也没发生。回去的一路上你不停回头，什么也一直没发生。|你拿了一个苹果。酸，非常酸，你赌着气把它吃完了。|你拿了一个，快步走开。回头看时，摊子不见了，碗和蜡烛也一起不见了。}

@event nm_dawn_packing
# en: Before the Light
title [b8e9c5] = 天亮之前
# en: {~Towards dawn the market packs up all at once, as if on a signal you didn't hear. An old seller is fighting a canvas roof that wants to stay up.|The sky is going grey and the stalls are coming down. One old woman with a cart of crates is a long way behind everyone else.|First light is an hour off and the market is leaving. A seller with a bad hand is trying to rope a crate one-handed.}
text [dda753] = {~天快亮时，集市一下子全收摊了，像是收到了一个你没听见的信号。一个老卖家正跟一块怎么也不肯放下的帆布顶棚较劲。|天色发灰，摊子纷纷拆下。一个推着一车箱子的老太太远远落在所有人后面。|离天亮还有一个钟头，集市就要走了。一个手有伤的卖家正试着用一只手捆箱子。}
# en: A night market folding itself away in the grey before dawn, stallholders packing crates, one old seller struggling with a canvas roof.
scene [f89773] = 天亮前灰蒙蒙的光里，夜市正收拢起来，摊主们打包箱子，一个老卖家对付着一块帆布顶棚。
# en: Help them pack
opt.left.label [96db79] = 帮他们收拾
# en: {~You wrestle the canvas down together and rope the crates. The seller presses a coin and a sugared plum on you. You run for the castle as the sky goes pink.|You load the cart while she tells you, in great detail, about a market in a country you've never heard of. She pays you in coin and gossip. You're late back.|You rope the crates. He watches, nods, and pays you a coin from a country that doesn't exist, and one from this one. The sun's nearly up when you climb in at the window.}
opt.left.say.1 [93b6d5] = {~你们一起把帆布拽下来，捆好箱子。卖家塞给你一枚硬币和一颗糖渍李子。天边泛粉时你往城堡跑。|你帮她装车，她详详细细地给你讲一个你从没听说过的国家里的集市。她用硬币和闲话付了你钱。你回去晚了。|你捆好箱子。他看着，点点头，付了你一枚不存在的国家的硬币，还有一枚这儿的。你从窗户爬进去时，太阳都快出来了。}
# en: Slip home before the light
opt.right.label [ea0686] = 天亮前溜回去
# en: {~You leave them to it and slip back in the grey. Behind you, the field is already only a field.|You go while it's still dark enough to go. At the stile you look back: no stalls, no lanterns, no carts.|You're in bed before the light, and from the window the far field is empty grass, as if you'd dreamt it.}
opt.right.say.1 [a247be] = {~你随他们去，在灰蒙蒙里溜回去。身后的田野已经只是一片田野了。|你趁天还够黑的时候走。到篱阶回头看：没有摊子，没有灯笼，没有车。|天亮前你已躺在床上，从窗户望去，远田是一片空草地，像是你做了个梦。}

@event nm_moon_scales
# en: A Pound of Moonlight
title [1dbe10] = 一磅月光
# en: {~A seller is weighing moonlight on brass scales: a pale powder that glows and weighs slightly less than nothing. "From the last full moon," he says. "Good for spellwork. Or for lying about having done the spellwork."|A moonlight-seller is arguing with a customer about whether his scales are honest. They are not. Neither is the customer.|"Moonlight," says the man at the scales, "for a student who's behind." He looks at you meaningfully. You are, a little.}
text [1525d0] = {~一个卖家正用黄铜秤称月光：一种发光的淡色粉末，比什么都没有还要轻一点。“上个满月的，”他说，“施法好用。或者用来谎称你施过法。”|一个卖月光的正跟顾客争他的秤准不准。秤不准。顾客也不老实。|“月光，”秤边的男人说，“给落了功课的学生。”他意味深长地看着你。你确实落了一点。}
# en: A night stall of brass scales weighing a pale glowing powder, the seller arguing with a customer over the weight.
scene [ebcdbf] = 夜市摊上的黄铜秤称着一种发光的淡色粉末，卖家正跟顾客为分量争执。
# en: Buy a pinch for your studies
opt.left.label [b01def] = 买一撮帮你学习
# en: {~You dust it on your notes. For a week the hard parts glow, faintly, until you've learned them.|You sprinkle it in your inkwell. Everything you write that week sticks, the way moonlight sticks to water.|It smells of cold stone. You study by it for three nights and, to your surprise, remember all of it.}
opt.left.say.1 [c2d072] = {~你把它撒在笔记上。一个星期里，难的地方都微微发光，直到你学会为止。|你把它撒进墨水瓶。那个星期你写下的东西都记得牢牢的，就像月光粘在水上。|它有一股冷石头的味道。你借着它读了三个晚上，出乎意料地全记住了。}
# en: Call out his crooked scales
opt.right.label [edb14b] = 揭穿他的歪秤
# en: {~You show the customer the wax under the scale-pan. The seller scrapes it off with his thumbnail, weighs her moonlight again, and gives you a pinch of it for your trouble, scowling.|You point out the bent beam. He straightens it with a sigh, as if you'd taken a tooth, and the next three customers get honest weight.|"Sharp eyes," he says, and turns the scales so you can watch him make them true. "Come and work for me." You decline.}
opt.right.say.1 [481556] = {~你让顾客看秤盘下面的蜡。卖家用拇指甲把它刮掉，重新给她称了月光，又沉着脸送了你一撮，算是你的辛苦费。|你指出秤杆是弯的。他叹了口气，像是被你拔了颗牙，把秤杆掰直，接下来三个顾客都拿到了足秤。|“眼睛真尖，”他说，把秤转过来让你看着他把它校准。“来给我干活吧。”你谢绝了。}
# en: {~He tells you the scales are fine and your eyes are crooked. The customer agrees with him.|He weighs your accusation and finds it light. Everyone at the stall laughs.|"Prove it," he says, and you can't. You leave lighter by some pride.}
opt.right.say.2 [17c521] = {~他说秤没问题，是你眼睛歪了。顾客也站在他那边。|他掂了掂你的指控，觉得太轻。摊前的人都笑了。|“证明给我看，”他说，你证明不了。你走的时候，少了点面子。}
